prov.ttl is the W3C PROV-O ontology, retrieved from https://www.w3.org/ns/prov.ttl on
2026-10-08 and redistributed under the W3C Software and Document Notice and License.

It is vendored here, and deliberately not in Fieldwork, so that the ontology check can
reason over the axioms Fieldwork's vocabulary relies on without the application fetching
anything at run time. Fieldwork reuses PROV-O terms but declares no owl:imports, so a
reasoner given only Fieldwork's files cannot see that prov:Entity and prov:Activity are
disjoint. Merging this file is what makes a cross-kind conflation detectable.
